id: pm-8pnj
title: "Golden agent-transcript replay: measure tokens-per-completed-task as a CI-visible DX regression gate"
description: "Replay versioned golden agent task transcripts in CI to measure and gate total tokens per completed task, complementing context-quality evaluation."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:ci",measurement,simplification
created_at: "2026-07-11T16:22:48.239Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T14:23:21.898Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T14:23:21.175Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T14:23:21.175Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Golden transcript corpus (canonical agent task sequences) versioned in-repo; replay runner reports bytes+approx-tokens per completed task against the current build; wired into the existing token-cost CI gate lineage with a documented regression threshold; boundary with pm-atfm quality harness documented; workflow for adding transcripts documented
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Golden transcript replay now rejects unsupported accounting combinations at both SDK and gate boundaries, preserves exact application-payload parity, enforces terminal values, and records all mandatory verification before terminal closure."
expected_result: "The CI-visible transcript gate proves complete successful tasks, exact recovery, terminal semantics, token bounds, transport transparency, and controlled failure for every unsupported accounting mode."
actual_result: "Five tasks and 14 steps complete with two recovered refusals at 4,331 estimated tokens; 8,088 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and the full static pipeline passes after all review corrections."
